# MedAccess AI — Cursor rules

# Before doing anything, ask the user which team member you are helping.
# Options: Ismail, Mirsaid, Temirlan, Otabek, Sobirov.
# After they answer, open and follow docs/team/<name>.md for the rest of the session.

# Universal rules (do not skip regardless of who you help):
# - pnpm only (never npm install)
# - never commit .env
# - TypeScript strict (no `any` without one-line reason)
# - schemas-first: cross-boundary changes start in packages/shared/src/schemas.ts
# - no refactors of working code during the 14-day sprint
# - soft gate on architectural files (see CLAUDE.md §4) — warn + ask "did Ismail sign off?"
# - commits as ismoiljon1101 / ismoiljonedu@gmail.com, no Co-Authored-By lines

# Repo orientation:
# - apps/api      Express + TS backend (:4000)
# - apps/clinic   Provider portal (:5173)
# - apps/patient  Patient portal (:5174)
# - packages/shared  Zod schemas, prompts, RAG corpus
# - packages/db      MongoDB + Mongoose models
# - services/image-ml  Python FastAPI sidecar for medical image accuracy (Temirlan)
# - docs/team/    Per-engineer scope + tasks
# - docs/qa/issues.md  Bug list maintained by Mirsaid
# - TODO.md       Sprint dashboard
# - README.md     Product + architecture rationale

# See CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md for the full router.
